# The corners of the map's rectangle in the scenario editor's map size dialog.
# Each is dragged in turn, which changes two of the four numbers below the
# map; editor_dialogs.script drags the rectangle as a whole. OK then gives
# the scenario its new size, which the dialog shows when it is opened again.
# args: -EDITOR
at 201 rclick 400 150
at 241 key DOWN
at 245 key DOWN
at 249 key DOWN
at 259 key RETURN
# The map is at 49,45 and 30 by 36 cells, a pixel a cell, in a board whose
# first cell is at 46,26.
at 301 press 124 106
at 310 move 132 110
at 320 move 140 115
at 330 shot bottom_right_held
at 331 release 140 115
at 360 shot bottom_right_moved
at 361 press 95 71
at 370 move 90 66
at 380 move 85 60
at 390 release 85 60
at 420 shot top_left_moved
at 421 press 140 60
at 430 move 145 65
at 440 shot top_right_held
at 441 release 145 65
at 470 shot top_right_moved
at 471 press 85 115
at 480 move 80 120
at 490 release 80 120
at 520 shot bottom_left_moved
at 521 click 67 203
at 580 shot map_after_ok
# The menu opens on Size Map, the line it was left on.
at 581 rclick 400 150
at 621 key RETURN
at 660 shot dialog_again
at 661 quit
